# ⚡ capture-help

> A fast, modern, project-aware terminal AI assistant powered by the official DeepSeek API. Built with Python, Typer, Rich, and the OpenAI SDK.

---

## 🚀 Key Features

- **🧠 Project Intelligence & Codebase Questioning (`capture-help ask "<question>"`)**:
  - Automatically detects Git repository root and project metadata (Languages, Build System, Frameworks).
  - Indexes project files and matches relevant code snippets to answer codebase questions with exact file citations.
- **🔀 Unix Stdin Pipe Support**:
  - Seamlessly accepts stdin input:
    - `make 2>&1 | capture-help explain`
    - `cat error.log | capture-help explain`
    - `git diff | capture-help review`
    - `git diff | capture-help commit`
- **🛠️ Interactive Diff Patching (`capture-help fix main.cpp`)**:
  - Displays a clean syntax-highlighted diff (`a/file` vs `b/file`) and asks `Apply this change? (y/N)`.
  - Automatically patches files and creates a `.bak` backup upon confirmation.
- **⚡ Token Usage & Real-Time Cost Tracking**:
  - Displays request generation time, input/output token counts, estimated cost ($0.14/1M input, $0.28/1M output), and model name.
- **📜 Session History & Resuming (`capture-help history` / `capture-help resume <id>`)**:
  - Persists chat conversations to disk. Resume prior sessions seamlessly.
- **⚡ Shell Aliases (`capture-help alias --install`)**:
  - Installs shell shortcuts (`ai`, `aiask`, `aifix`, `aireview`, `aidoc`, `aicommit`) into `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`.

---

## 🚀 Quick Start & Installation

### Option 1: Install locally in editable mode

```bash
git clone https://github.com/capture/capture-help.git
cd capture-help
pip install -e .
```

### Option 2: Run with Virtual Environment

```bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
```

---

## ⚙️ Configuration

Set your DeepSeek API key using the interactive configuration manager:

```bash
capture-help config
```

Or set `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` in your environment or `.env` file:

```env
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your_deepseek_api_key_here
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
DEFAULT_PROVIDER=deepseek
```

---

## 🛠️ Command Reference

| Command | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `capture-help ask "<question>"` | Ask a question about your entire codebase using automatic project indexing. |
| `capture-help chat` | Interactive AI terminal chat with project context & session persistence. |
| `capture-help explain [file|log]` | Explain source files or analyze compiler/build logs (or pipe via stdin). |
| `capture-help fix [file]` | Identify bugs and apply fixes with interactive syntax-highlighted diff patching. |
| `capture-help review [file|dir]` | Perform an automated code review with a visual Project Summary dashboard. |
| `capture-help docs [file]` | Generate technical documentation and docstrings. |
| `capture-help commit` | Read `git diff` or stdin and generate Conventional Commit messages. |
| `capture-help test [file]` | Generate unit tests for pytest, catch2, cargo test, etc. |
| `capture-help optimize [file]` | Analyze performance & memory bottlenecks with Big-O complexity. |
| `capture-help alias [--install]` | Generate or install shell aliases (`ai`, `aifix`, `aireview`, `aidoc`, `aicommit`). |
| `capture-help history` | List recent saved terminal chat sessions. |
| `capture-help resume <id>` | Resume a previous chat session by ID or index number. |
| `capture-help config` | View or update DeepSeek API key and base URL settings. |

---

## 💡 Workflow Examples

### 1. Ask Codebase Questions
```bash
capture-help ask "Where is GlassEffect initialized?"
```

### 2. Pipe Build Logs
```bash
make 2>&1 | capture-help explain
```

### 3. Interactive Diff Patching
```bash
capture-help fix main.cpp
# Output: Shows diff and asks: Apply this change to main.cpp? (y/N)
```

### 4. Code Review on Staged Git Diff
```bash
git diff --staged | capture-help review
```

